B.aYc={"Determine origin":0,"Determine cause":1,"Determine origin and cause":2,[u.eQ]:3,[u.cx]:4,[u.Z]:5,[u.m]:6,[u.hb]:7,[u.c7]:8,[u.al]:9,[u.cm]:10,[u.fr]:11,"Litigation / FRE 702 expert consultation":12,[u.fi]:13}
B.aX3=new A.bV(B.aYc,["Determine the origin. The investigator is asked to determine where the fire or explosion began, including the area of origin. This purpose is selected so that origin is a question in the assignment. It does not state where the fire or explosion began.","Determine the cause. The investigator is asked to determine the circumstances that resulted in the fire or explosion, including how an ignition source and the fuel first ignited came together. This purpose is selected so that cause remains a question in the assignment. It does not state what caused the fire or explosion.","Determine origin and cause. The investigator is asked to determine both where the fire or explosion began and the circumstances that resulted in it, including how an ignition source and the fuel first ignited came together. This purpose is selected so that both questions are in the assignment. It does not state a location or what caused the fire or explosion.","Determine how the fire or explosion developed or spread. The investigator is asked to determine the development or spread, including paths and conditions that affected it. This purpose is selected so that development and spread are questions in the assignment. It does not describe a path or a sequence on this scene.","Evaluate ignition source, first fuel, and competent ignition. The investigator is asked to evaluate candidate ignition sources, the fuel first ignited, and whether a source was competent to ignite that fuel. This purpose is selected so that those questions are in the assignment. It does not name a source or a fuel, and it does not state that ignition was competent.","Assess responsibility and contributing human factors. The investigator is asked to assess human factors that may bear on responsibility, including acts, omissions, or conditions within this assignment. This purpose is selected so that those questions are in the assignment. It does not assign responsibility to any person.","Classify the incident. The investigator is asked to classify the incident, when the investigation supports a classification, as accidental, natural, incendiary, or undetermined. This purpose is selected so that classification is a question in the assignment. It does not state which class applies.","Address death or injury related to the fire or explosion. The investigator is asked to include any death or injury related to the fire or explosion, and the circumstances that would connect it to the event, within this assignment. This purpose is selected so that those questions are in the assignment. It does not state that a death or an injury occurred.","Analyze product, equipment, or system failure. The investigator is asked to analyze whether a product, piece of equipment, or system failed in a way that is within this assignment. This purpose is selected so that failure analysis is a question in the assignment. It does not state that any product, equipment, or system failed.","Evaluate fire protection, detection, or suppression performance. The investigator is asked to evaluate the performance of fire protection, detection, or suppression systems to the extent that performance is within this assignment. This purpose is selected so that system performance is a question in the assignment. It does not state how any system performed.","Support evidence identification, documentation, or collection. The investigator is asked to support identifying, documenting, or collecting evidence within this assignment. This purpose is selected so that this evidence work is within the assignment. It does not list items or state what any item shows.","Conduct peer review or independent technical review. The investigator is asked to review the technical work of the investigation independently, within this assignment. This purpose is selected so that review is within the assignment. It does not state the result of a review.","Provide litigation and FRE 702 consultation. The investigator is asked to consult on the questions in this assignment, including questions that may be offered under Federal Rule of Evidence 702. This purpose is selected so that the consultation stays inside that scope. It does not state an opinion.","Address codes, standards, or prevention recommendations. The investigator is asked to address codes, standards, or prevention measures that are within this assignment. This purpose is selected so that those questions are in the assignment. It does not state that a requirement was violated or name a prevention measure for this scene."],t.li)
